ketexon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T21:52:41Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T23:39:36Z","body":"Since I cannot attach an abstract script to a Node, the only way I could get this to work is by adding a normal script to an object *then* making it abstract. This isn't caught by the scene tree *immediately*, and you only get a hint of an error when you run the scene, which causes the \"should not be abstract\" error. ~~I do not get the same error with the empty \"attach script\", but I do get the error with undoing.~~\n\nHowever, **when you reload the scene,** **it removes the script** with the \"should not be abstract\" error and **does not show that the scene file has changed**, even though it has. This could be bad, since saving silently causes whatever properties were on that script to be lost. \n\nNot to extend the discussion too much, but would it be possible to have the ability to set the script to an abstract script, and have it be a runtime error and a Node configuration warning in the Editor? I'd expect it would be relatively common to make existing script abstract, so this would be a worthwhile addition. This would also allow \"base scenes\" to have abstract scripts, allowing inherited scenes to attach a concrete script.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141444699/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141481646","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109171#issuecomment-3141481646","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109171","id":3141481646,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67PzSu","user":{"login":"jramonrod","id":9137143,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzcxNDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9137143?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod","html_url":"https://github.com/jramonrod","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T22:11:07Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T22:11:39Z","body":">Since I cannot attach an abstract script to a Node, the only way I could get this to work is by adding a normal script to an object then making it abstract. \n\nYou mean you could not reproduce my scenario? The MRP I submitted should already have it happening. If we right click on the child node of the scene we'll see the missing \"Extend script...\" option.\n\n>Not to extend the discussion too much, but would it be possible to have the ability to set the script to an abstract script, and have it be a runtime error and a Node configuration warning in the Editor? \n\nSpeaking more towards the solution space of things I would support that!! ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141481646/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141652058","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109171#issuecomment-3141652058","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109171","id":3141652058,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67Qc5a","user":{"login":"ketexon","id":29184562,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTg0NTYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29184562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon","html_url":"https://github.com/ketexon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ketexon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T23:44:58Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T23:48:06Z","body":"> You mean you could not reproduce my scenario? The MRP I submitted should already have it happening. If we right click on the child node of the scene we'll see the missing \"Extend script...\" option.\n\nAh wait I see it now. I was messing around with the script property rather than a node with a custom type (which I did not know were different!), but both have (probably related) issues. I bet the issue with the menu item is that the node is marked as having a custom type, so it doesn't show the normal Attach/Detach script buttons, but the custom type cannot be resolved, so it also doesn't show the Extend script button, leaving an empty section in the menu.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141652058/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3144122426","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109171#issuecomment-3144122426","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109171","id":3144122426,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67Z4A6","user":{"login":"jramonrod","id":9137143,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzcxNDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9137143?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod","html_url":"https://github.com/jramonrod","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T10:42:52Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T10:43:04Z","body":">I bet the issue with the menu item is that the node is marked as having a custom type, so it doesn't show the normal Attach/Detach script buttons, but the custom type cannot be resolved, so it also doesn't show the Extend script button\n\nYes! I am new to the repository so I haven't looked into the code but that very likely seems to be the case!\nWould also explain how on hover it only says \"Node\" for the type instead of the abstract type it is underlying it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3144122426/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3148732638","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109171#issuecomment-3148732638","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109171","id":3148732638,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67rdje","user":{"login":"jramonrod","id":9137143,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzcxNDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9137143?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod","html_url":"https://github.com/jramonrod","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jramonrod/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-03T22:13:03Z","updated_at":"2025-08-03T22:13:03Z","body":"Btw wanted to add to the conversation I noticed this while working today other engine-native abstract classes are actually greyed out. A similar behaviour would probably be desirable in this menu. This doesn't address the scenario that @ketexon laid out, of making the script abstract _afterwards_. But it nevertheless is probably desirable behaviour. Also cool that it provides a small text doc.\n\n<img width=\"983\" height=\"763\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b3a82ceb-653d-42bd-babf-9f5cb459ba8d\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3148732638/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3216552487","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109171#issuecomment-3216552487","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109171","id":3216552487,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_uLIn","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"